# SPA routing.
#
# Every path in this app is client-side: /rules/blackpowder and
# /warbands/<id>/print are React Router destinations, not files on disk. Without
# this rule, opening one directly — a bookmark, a shared roster link, a refresh —
# is a 404, because the host looks for a file that was never built.
#
# 200 rather than 301/302: the URL must stay as typed so the router can read it.
# A redirect would rewrite the address bar to / and lose the destination.
#
# Read by Cloudflare Pages and by Netlify alike, which is why it lives here
# rather than only in netlify.toml. Static files are matched first by both, so
# this catches only what genuinely has no file behind it.
/*  /index.html  200
